        "title": "About Sudan Conflict",
        "subject": "Sudan Conflict",
        "summary": "The Sudan conflict is an ongoing armed struggle that began on 15 April 2023 between the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF), led by Abdel Fattah al-Burhan, and the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF), led by Mohamed Hamdan Dagalo. What began with fighting in and around Khartoum rapidly spread across Sudan, including Darfur and Kordofan, causing a nationwide humanitarian and displacement crisis and extensive damage to civilian infrastructure.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "label": "Start date and principal parties",
            "value": "Armed hostilities began on 15 April 2023 between the SAF and the RSF; the conflict followed a power struggle and disagreements linked to security-sector reform and the proposed integration of the RSF into the regular armed forces.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o1",
              "o2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Geographic scope",
            "value": "The conflict began in Khartoum and Merowe and quickly engulfed Darfur; it has since affected much of Sudan, with Khartoum, Darfur and Kordofan among the principal conflict-affected regions.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o3",
              "o4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Political context",
            "value": "The war interrupted efforts to restore a civilian-led transition after Sudan's October 2021 military coup, following the 2019 overthrow of former president Omar al-Bashir.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Humanitarian impact",
            "value": "UN agencies describe the conflict as driving mass internal and cross-border displacement, acute hunger, and severely constrained access to essential services such as water, health care and shelter.",
